    "conclusion": "The exact VM exposes a callable SPTM oracle for IA/DA user-pointer signing and authentication under the supplied discriminator. The target-context probe resolves the exact worker thread and reproduces a real thread-state PAC consumer under its live jop_pid, and the identity-gated Cyanide VM adapter reproduces that consumer through the existing lab KRW transport. Independently, the public FROM_SELF converter produced reply-compatible PC/LR PAC for same-task and transferred cross-task thread control rights without KRW or kcall. The corrected repeated scope run does not establish strict process isolation, and stock acquisition of a sufficient target thread control right remains unproven. This does not establish arbitrary kernel-pointer signing, executable-memory modification, or an SPTM write primitive."
